    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S1343B\n\nSPONSOR: BROOKS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act relating to the acquisition of real property by eminent domain\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to enable the sale of certain portions and\nterritories of New York American Water located in Nassau County to the\nMassapequa Water District.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. amends the town law to provide that the acquisition of prop-\nerty by eminent domain by towns and water districts that are special\nassessing units as defined by a waterworks corporation tariff as of May\nfirst 2019 in a county of one million one hundred thousand residents or\nmore under the jurisdiction of of the public service commission shall\nonly pay compensation in proceedings brought pursuant subdivision two of\nsection sixty-four of subdivision five of section two hundred fifteen of\nthe town law if the state supreme court solely utilizes an income\ncapitalization method of valuation based on the actual net income, and\nupon the court's determination of the amount based on the aforementioned\nmethod and the entry of final judgement, filing of final decree, and\nconclusion of any appeal related to the condemnation process has been\ncompleted. Further, if a court shall utilize any method of compensation\nother than the income capitalization method or if the proposed compen-\nsation is more than the rate base of the assets taken in condemnation as\nutilized by the public service commission the town or water district may\nwithdraw the condemnation proceeding without prejudice or costs to any\nparty.\n\nSection 2. is the enacting clause.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation would enable the Massapequa Water District located in\nthe county of Nassau to make a good faith effort to purchase certain\nterritories from New York American Water with the risk of financial\njeopardy should the sale not be possible. The provisions laid forth by\nthis legislation is similar to that of what is known as conditional\ncondemnation that Water Authorities currently utilized.  The enactment\nof this legislation and sale of these territories would result in a cost\nreduction for all ratepayers affected.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
